---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Contact VixenBliss Agency for support, legal requests, business inquiries, and creative technology questions."
>
  <p>
    VixenBliss Agency welcomes clear, professional inquiries related to the website, business opportunities, support,
    legal questions, and creative technology collaboration. The best way to reach us is by email, which helps us route
    each message to the right context and respond with the information needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    We aim to keep communication practical and respectful. When contacting us, please include enough detail for us to
    understand the request, such as the relevant page, topic, company name if applicable, and the best email address for
    a reply.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    Contact VixenBliss Agency at
    <a href="mailto:support@vixenbliss.com">support@vixenbliss.com</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This address can be used for support, legal communications, privacy requests, business inquiries, provider questions,
    and general website feedback.
  </p>
  <p>
    Using one visible contact address keeps the public channel simple while still allowing us to classify each message
    internally by topic and urgency.
  </p>

  <h2>Support Requests</h2>
  <p>
    For support questions, include a short description of what happened and where it occurred. Helpful details may
    include the page URL, device type, browser, approximate time of the issue, and whether the problem happened once or
    repeatedly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Support requests may relate to page loading, media playback, broken links, display issues, accessibility barriers,
    or other technical behavior on the public website. We use this information to investigate and improve reliability.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal and Privacy Requests</h2>
  <p>
    Legal and privacy communications should clearly state the nature of the request. This may include questions about
    our Privacy Policy, Cookie Policy, Terms of Service, data rights, provider information, or public website practices.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a request involves personal information connected to a specific email address, we may need to verify that the
    requester is authorized to receive or modify that information. This helps protect privacy and prevent unauthorized
    access.
  </p>

  <h2>Business Inquiries</h2>
  <p>
    For business inquiries, please include your name, organization, website if available, and a brief explanation of the
    opportunity. Useful context may include timeline, market, campaign goals, creative needs, technical requirements, or
    the type of collaboration you have in mind.
  </p>
  <p>
    We review business messages for fit and clarity. Not every inquiry will lead to a collaboration, but a concise and
    specific message helps us respond more effectively.
  </p>

  <h2>Creative and Technology Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about AI-assisted visual content, media workflows, content management, or digital presentation are also
    welcome. We are especially interested in conversations that connect visual direction with practical implementation:
    fast pages, organized content, reliable delivery, and clear brand communication.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your question concerns a specific page or asset, include the relevant link and describe what you want to know.
    This helps us avoid guessing and gives the conversation a better starting point.
  </p>

  <h2>Website Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    We also accept feedback about the public website experience. This may include comments about readability, navigation,
    mobile display, media loading, footer links, or information that could be clearer for visitors and campaign
    reviewers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Useful feedback is specific and calm: tell us what page you were viewing, what you expected to happen, and what you
    saw instead. Screenshots are helpful when the issue is visual, but avoid sending anything private or unnecessary.
  </p>

  <h2>Response Expectations</h2>
  <p>
    We try to review incoming messages in a reasonable timeframe, but response times may vary depending on volume,
    complexity, and whether the request requires technical or legal review. Sending duplicate messages may slow down the
    process, so one clear email is usually best.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please do not send confidential business information, credentials, payment details, or unnecessary personal data by
    email. If sensitive context is required, we will coordinate an appropriate next step.
  </p>

  <h2>Company Information</h2>
  <p>
    VixenBliss Agency operates as a creative technology and visual media platform. Public information about our privacy
    practices, site terms, and cookie use is available through the footer links on every page.
  </p>
  <p>
    For all contact categories, use
    <a href="mailto:support@vixenbliss.com">support@vixenbliss.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
